# Served by Cloudflare Workers static assets. Everything defaults to
# `max-age=0, must-revalidate`, which makes a browser re-check every file on
# every page view. Cheap per file, but a repeat visit on a slow connection
# spends dozens of round trips on 304s before anything renders.
#
# Only the build output is overridden here. Next puts a content hash in these
# filenames, so a changed file gets a new name and the old one can never go
# stale. That is exactly what `immutable` promises.
#
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Photos that go through Image Transformations (src/lib/imageLoader.ts) get
# an hour. Below that, Cloudflare resizes "with reduced effort" and barely
# keeps the result ("cache-control is too restrictive"). Not longer: the
# filenames are stable, so a replaced photo can show its old self until the
# max-age runs out, and an hour is the most we accept. Purging the photo's
# URL clears Cloudflare's copies at once. The hero files are not resized and
# keep the default.
/products/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/about/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/instagram/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/logo_black.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# No other site may show ours in a frame, which is how clickjacking works.
# `frame-ancestors` is the current standard, `X-Frame-Options` the older one.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
